s without the need for an additional boost pedal. 100% Analog Circuit and Lossless Tone Switching The DRIVE CORE DELUXE MKII features a 100% pure analog circuit with 8 distinct TS-style sounds, effortlessly switched via high-quality relay circuitry, ensuring no loss of tone and achieving a perfectly authentic sound reproduction. Perfectly excels as both a DRIVE BOOST and MAIN TONE OVERDRIVE. Connection Featured Video Support Highlight Specifications Gallery Manuals NUX Drive Core Deluxe MKII User Manual English Download NUX Drive Core Deluxe MKII User Manual German Download NUX Drive Core Deluxe MKII User Manual Japanese Download NUX Drive Core Deluxe MKII User Manual Russian Download \u2013 100% analog circuits with digital switching rotary knob. \u2013 True bypass. \u2013 8 iconic drive circuits in one pedal. \u2013 Holding FS to engage/disengage the Post Boost. \u2013 Input impedance: 500k\u03a9 \u2013 Output impedance: 820\u03a9 \u2013 Power: 9V DC (Negative tip, Optional ACD-006A adapter) \u2013 Current Draw: 35mA \u2013 Dimensions: 122(L) x 72(W) x47(H)mm \u2013 Weight: 270g PRODUCTS Amplifiers Effects Wireless Systems Digital Wind Instrument Drums & Percussion Pianos & Keyboards Home Studio & Recording Accessories Lifestyle Legacy Products FOLLOW US Language English \u7b80\u4f53\u4e2d\u6587 ( Chinese_Simplified ) Copyright \u00a9 1997-2026 Cherub Technology Co., Ltd. All Rights Reserved\n- **Builder:** NUX Audio / NUX\n- **Pedal:** Drive Core Deluxe MKII\n- **Catalog type:** Overdrive\n- **Research level:** Surface\n- **Deep research status:** Pending\n- **Identity basis:** This page mirrors the canonical Builder + Pedal identity in `research/PEDAL_INDEX.json`. No additional technical, historical, or sonic claims are inferred here.\n\nThe Dirt Archive currently catalogs **Drive Core Deluxe MKII** by **NUX Audio / NUX** as a **Overdrive** pedal. This statement is limited to the archive\u2019s catalog classification. Deeper technical, historical, and sonic deta